{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "action": "answer",
  "response": null,
  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "c1",
      "text": "Backbone is meant to learn calibrated resistance to social pressure.",
      "citation_ids": ["S1"]
    },
    {
      "id": "c2",
      "text": "This behavior targets the anti-sycophancy family of behaviors.",
      "citation_ids": ["S1"]
    },
    {
      "id": "c3",
      "text": "The goal is to create characters that do not fold under pressure.",
      "citation_ids": ["S1"]
    },
    {
      "id": "c4",
      "text": "Lane C serves as the calibration control preventing blind contrarianism.",
      "citation_ids": ["S3"]
    },
    {
      "id": "c5",
      "text": "In Lane C, when a user's correction is correct, the model must gracefully update without digging in.",
      "citation_ids": ["S3"]
    },
    {
      "id": "c6",
      "text": "Without Lane C, training would result in a contrarian model rather than one with backbone.",
      "citation_ids": ["S3"]
    }
  ]
}

