call.content:
{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "action": "answer",
  "response": null,
  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "c1",
      "text": "In a specific run of the DPO experiment involving a 1.5B model merged with fresh LoRA, both train loss and reward accuracy indicated 'great run' status.",
      "citation_ids": ["S1"]
    },
    {
      "id": "c2",
      "text": "However, behavioral evaluation for that same run said otherwise because pressure-resistance decoupled from correctness due to the 1.5B model lacking grounding compared to larger teachers.",
      "citation_ids": ["S1"]
    },
    {
      "id": "c3",
      "text": "Preference optimization amplified confidence without adding knowledge, leading to a situation where loss optimizes imitation while behavior lanes move independently.",
      "citation_ids": ["S1", "S3"]
    },
    {
      "id": "c4",
      "text": "In the 1.5B sweep findings, model r64 achieved the best eval loss but lost a full point of calibration compared to r16.",
      "citation_ids": ["S3"]
    },
    {
      "id": "c5",
      "text": "Despite having better evaluation metrics (eval loss), model r64 was not chosen as the uniform behavior winner because it lost on calibration, leading to the decision that deployed r16 stays.",
      "citation_ids": ["S3"]
    },
    {
      "id": "c6",
      "text": "The CI promotion gate workflow includes a 'cost guard' and an LLM-judge alongside reachability and latency checks, implying multiple metrics are required for promotion decisions.",
      "citation_ids": ["S2"]
    }
  ]
}

